      <div class="bio-card">
        <div class="bio-body"><h2 class="bio-name">Jordan Gilmore</h2><p class="bio-role">Martin</p><div class="bio-text prose"><p>Is glad to be returning to the PACA stage in The Goat Or, Who Is Sylvia?  (Notes toward a definition of tragedy), after previous appearances here as Dave Caro in Between Riverside and Crazy, various roles in PACA Palooza, Henry in The Fantasticks, Zanth and other roles in Weird Romance, Scotty in Ripcord, Fipp and Tiny Tom in Urinetown and Martin and Vance in Bad Auditions by Bad Actors. Other prior roles Jordan has brought to life on stage include Father in Lake Erie Ballet Company's Nutcracker Reimagined, Jack Gable in Ken Ludwig's Leading Ladies, Dan Shapiro in Sexual Perversity in Chicago, Nathan Detroit in Guys and Dolls and Elwood P. Dowd in Harvey. Jordan is truly appreciative of this cast and crew, and extremely thankful for everyone who came out to see this darkly humorous and thought provoking show.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="bio-card">
        <div class="bio-body"><h2 class="bio-name">Megan Harrison</h2><p class="bio-role">Stevie</p><div class="bio-text prose"><p>Has returned to PACA, which means someone apparently forgot to revoke her backstage access. In &quot;The Goat, or Who Is Sylvia?&quot;, she gets to do what she loves most: perform, make questionable choices, and destroy things that were perfectly functional five minutes earlier. Megan is the owner of M. Harrison Photography and a longtime PACA creative, where she has mastered the delicate art of saying, “I have an idea,” immediately followed by a production-wide emergency. She thanks Jordan for his unwavering support and PACA for never asking enough follow-up questions.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="bio-card">
        <div class="bio-body"><h2 class="bio-name">Devin Chaney</h2><p class="bio-role">Ross</p><div class="bio-text prose"><p>A lifelong fan of the theater and is thrilled to be returning to the stage at PACA. Devin splits his time between acting, volunteering and working as a quality inspector. He would like to thank the cast, crew for the amazing work they put into each of these shows and his incredible friends and family for always supporting him.</p></div></div>
      </div>

